# E-723: If there is a finite projective plane of order $n$ then must $n$ be a prime power? A finite projective plane of order $n$ is a collection of subsets of $\{1,\ldots,n^2+n+1\}$ of size $n+1$ such that every pair of elements is contained in exactly one set.
